{
  "summary": "This experiment replaced avgpool with transformer aggregation in the current best multimodal pipeline (scvi_n200, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion), a single-variable change from config_037, achieving a validation accuracy of 0.725 and F1 of 0.685, a ~1.9-point accuracy and ~1.8-point F1 improvement over the avgpool baseline (0.706 acc / 0.667 F1). This contrasts with the near-null result (~0.3 pts) observed for the same aggregation swap in the RNA-only setting, suggesting that transformer aggregation extracts profile-level structure that is specifically beneficial when the RNA representation is subsequently fused with image features via weighted fusion, though the mechanism behind this interaction remains unverified. It is uncertain whether the ~1.9-point gain is robust across random seeds, whether further headroom exists above 0.725 from other unexplored axes (e.g., attention-based fusion, alternative encoder combinations), and whether the aggregation–fusion interaction generalizes beyond the current configuration."
}

